SSPS Novelty Verifier™

“Scan your ideas before the world does.”

🔍 Purpose:

A forensic-grade pre-vault scan module that determines whether an idea or system you’re about to document is:

✅ Novel (not already published)

🚨 Not mirrored by others yet

⚖️ Enforceable (no conflicting prior art or disqualifying derivative claims)

🛠️ Functional Overview
Component	Function
🧠 Semantic AI Agent	Reads your IP draft (text, image, or code) and interprets it into core logic functions
🌍 Web Scanner	Scans the open internet, GitHub, ArXiv, patents, company whitepapers, and public APIs
🔬 Prior Art Comparator	Uses vector similarity + structural mapping to compare against known prior art databases
📈 Contradiction Analyzer	Detects false originality claims by others if they mirror logic after your timestamps
🧾 Legal Pre-Report Generator	Outputs PDF or JSON with:

Novelty Score

Threat Map

Enforceability Index

Suggested Vault Protocols |
| 🔐 SSPS Enforcement Sync | Automatically suggests whether to:

Vault immediately

Delay and refine

Flag for internal containment

⚖️ What It Tells You
Result	What It Means	Action
🟢 High Novelty	No matching functions in public databases or filings	Proceed to Vault Forge
🟡 Moderate Novelty	Similar themes exist, but not structured or deployed the way you propose	Tweak language or process before vaulting
🔴 Conflict Detected	Public sources exist that could trigger a prior art challenge	Delay Vault, review matches, assign legal pathway
📂 Optional Inputs You Can Feed Into It

Raw idea descriptions

UX wireframes

Code logic or Python scripts

Data flow charts

Legal drafts

Artifacts (images, music, hardware design)

💎 Strategic Advantage for You

Saves time before vaulting IP that might have conflict.

Identifies false derivative actors trying to rush out mirror claims.

Auto-maps contradictions and alerts you to pre-existing disclosure risks.

Improves Vault Forge efficiency by streamlining what gets minted.

Prevents accidental dilution of tokenomics by vaulting something with public overlap.

